-- comments
1:1 plain -- A spread is `{` then `...` as the hole's first token, whatever comes
2:1 plain -- between them (frontend.md §9.1): `{ ...a }`, and a `{` whose `...` is on
3:1 plain -- the next line after a comment, both lex `l_brace ellipsis` and parse as
4:1 plain -- a `markup_spread`.
